says:
>
>   A few times on dying I have gotten these listed
>
>   Bad luck did not time out for you
>   Good luck did not time out for you
>
>   What does this mean in game terms, and how do you get luck timed?
>
>                                        Jorge
>
There was a luck item in your possession when you died.  You may or
may not have seen it in your inventory at the end of the game.
(For spoilage reasons, I won't say particularly which it is).

As far as "time out", your luck defaults to a rather neutral
status (plus or minus the phase of the moon).  Different things
you do may raise or lower your luck.  However, in the long term,
it will try to decay (i.e. time out) back towards zero.

When it says "...luck did not time out for you", it says that
whatever value your Luck happens to take on will hold firm
and not decay.  Good luck will remain as good luck.  Bad luck
will remain bad (until fixed otherwise).

Having Good luck not time out is a Very Desireable trait.
If your luck currently is good, hold onto this luck item.

Having bad luck not time out is very bad.  If you drop the
item, then everything is honky dory and it will decay towards
zero.

I'll let you guess for yourself what effect blessing and
cursing this item is likely to do.

